<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Nop.Data - second stage of the migration, immediately downstream of Nop.Core
    (Requirements 1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 1.4, 1.5, 2.4, 5.3).

    Converted from the classic (non-SDK) MSBuild format. Dropped in the conversion:
      * ToolsVersion / DefaultTargets / xmlns MSBuild 2003 attributes
      * ProjectGuid {CCD7F2C9-6A2C-4CF0-8E89-076B8FC0F144}, ProductVersion,
        SchemaVersion, FileAlignment, AppDesignerFolder, OutputType (Library is the
        SDK default), TargetFrameworkProfile
      * TargetFrameworkVersion v4.5.1
      * The Debug|AnyCPU / Release|AnyCPU PropertyGroup pair (the SDK supplies
        equivalent Debug/Release defaults) and the empty <PostBuildEvent/>
      * Import of $(MSBuildToolsPath)\Microsoft.CSharp.targets and the commented
        BeforeBuild/AfterBuild target stubs
      * The explicit <Compile Include="..."/> list of 128 files - replaced by the
        SDK's implicit globbing
      * BCL <Reference Include="System.*"/> entries (System, System.Core, System.Data,
        System.Xml, System.Xml.Linq, System.Data.DataSetExtensions, Microsoft.CSharp,
        System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations, System.Transactions, System.Web) -
        subsumed by the net10.0 shared framework. Note System.Web was referenced but
        never used: no source file under this project references System.Web,
        HttpContext, HostingEnvironment or HttpRuntime.
      * <Reference/> items with HintPaths into ..\..\packages\ (EntityFramework,
        EntityFramework.SqlServer, EntityFramework.SqlServerCompact,
        System.Data.SqlServerCe) - the packages.config surface, re-declared below as
        version-less <PackageReference/> items for the EF Core equivalents
      * <None Include="app.config"/> and <None Include="packages.config"/> - both
        files are deleted in this task

    Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs is retained (matching Nop.Core) and
    GenerateAssemblyInfo=false in src/Directory.Build.props keeps the SDK from
    emitting a duplicate set of assembly attributes.

    TargetFramework, Nullable, ImplicitUsings, GenerateAssemblyInfo and the shared
    assembly metadata come from src/Directory.Build.props; net10.0 is restated here so
    the target framework is verifiable from the project file itself (Requirement 1.2).
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    No <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" /> here.

    Nop.Core needs the ASP.NET Core shared framework because it consumes HttpContext /
    IHttpContextAccessor. Nop.Data does not: a grep of every .cs file under this
    project for System.Web, HttpContext, HostingEnvironment and HttpRuntime returns no
    matches, and the only non-BCL namespaces used are System.Data.Entity* (ported to
    EF Core below) plus Nop.Core.*. Everything else it uses - System.Data.Common,
    System.Transactions, System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations, System.Reflection - is
    in the Microsoft.NETCore.App shared framework that the SDK references by default.
    The legacy <Reference Include="System.Web" /> was an unused leftover.
  -->

  <!--
    packages.config -> PackageReference (Requirements 1.3, 1.5).

    Versions are governed centrally by src/Directory.Packages.props
    (ManagePackageVersionsCentrally=true, CentralPackageVersionOverrideEnabled=false),
    so every item below is intentionally version-less. All three already had
    <PackageVersion> entries (10.0.12); this task added none.

    Only DIRECT dependencies are declared. Each entry was verified against actual
    source usage (the EF6 namespace it replaces is shown, since the code port itself
    is task 3.2):

      Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore
          Replaces System.Data.Entity (12 files). DbContext/DbSet/ChangeTracker in
          NopObjectContext.cs, EfRepository.cs, IDbContext.cs;
          EntityTypeConfiguration -> IEntityTypeConfiguration in
          Mapping/NopEntityTypeConfiguration.cs and all 100+ Mapping/**/*Map.cs;
          Initializers/CreateTablesIfNotExist.cs; Extensions.cs;
          QueryableExtensions.cs.

      Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational
          Replaces System.Data.Entity.Infrastructure /
          System.Data.Entity.Core.{EntityClient,Objects,Metadata.Edm}. Supplies the
          raw-SQL and relational-metadata surface used directly by this project:
          NopObjectContext.ExecuteStoredProcedureList/SqlQuery/ExecuteSqlCommand
          (Database.SqlQuery / ExecuteSqlCommand -> FromSqlRaw / ExecuteSqlRaw),
          DbContextExtensions.DropPluginTable/GetTableName/GetColumnsMaxLength/DbName,
          and DataReaderExtensions.cs. Reachable transitively through
          ...SqlServer, but declared because Nop.Data binds against it directly.

      Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer
          Provider for SqlServerDataProvider.cs (replaces the EF6
          SqlConnectionFactory / Database.SetInitializer path) and the source of
          Microsoft.Data.SqlClient, which replaces the System.Data.SqlClient
          SqlParameter returned by SqlServerDataProvider.GetParameter().

    Dropped from the legacy packages.config and NOT restated:
      EntityFramework 6.1.3               superseded by the EF Core packages above
      EntityFramework.SqlServerCompact    SQL Server Compact has no EF Core provider
      Microsoft.SqlServer.Compact         and is removed from scope (design section 8);
                                          SqlCeDataProvider.cs is deleted in this task
                                          and SQL Server support is retained
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer" />
    <!--
      Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Proxies - restores EF6's DEFAULT lazy-loading
      behavior, which EF Core does not have (runtime deferral 4.7).

      EF6 proxied every entity automatically, so `public virtual` navigations on
      Nop.Core.Domain.** loaded on first touch. EF Core ships no proxy layer in the core
      package, so without this reference every navigation walk that has no explicit
      Include(...) returns null or an empty collection silently. This package supplies
      the Castle DynamicProxy-based entity proxies and the
      DbContextOptionsBuilder.UseLazyLoadingProxies() extension that
      NopObjectContext.OnConfiguring now calls unconditionally.

      Version-less, per this project's central-package-management convention; the pin
      (10.0.12, aligned with the EF Core pins) lives in src/Directory.Packages.props.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Proxies" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    ProjectReference to the already-migrated SDK-style Nop.Core (Requirement 2.4).
    The legacy <Project>{6BDA8332-...}</Project> and <Name>Nop.Core</Name> metadata
    children are dropped - the SDK resolves references by path.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Nop.Core\Nop.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
